swer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326338}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "84c10818-73ce-58a0-a3d2-b4c129acbe6d" :question/math-academy-id "q-38779" :question/problem "![](images/73/737052513985954a32dcce369fce60f898474db846319ca31b36e3e4682b4b37.png)\n\nThe graph of a polynomial $p(x)$ is shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $x=-4$ is a root of odd multiplicity.\n- $p(0)=3.$\n- $x=1$ is a root of odd multiplicity." :question/worked-solution "Let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. The root $x=-4$ has an even multiplicity because at $x=-4$ the graph just touches the $x$-axis and reverses direction.\n\n- Statement II is true. The graph passes through the $y$-axis at $y=3$, which means that $p(0)=3.$\n\n- Statement III is true. The root $x=1$ has an odd multiplicity because the graph passes through the $x$-axis at the point.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348356 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6c2785b2-559f-5363-85bc-7321b551a97d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346289} {:answer/id #uuid "738c7a23-f7aa-51f8-a828-559fb86be134" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346371} {:answer/id #uuid "e40b6b82-2faa-5fb1-8ee7-164e32650ad7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347358} {:answer/id #uuid "f19796ae-1350-577b-8f51-a061d4844c88" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347486} {:answer/id #uuid "f6c5884f-32c7-59e8-ac4e-487366b063ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I,II and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347538}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e40b6b82-2faa-5fb1-8ee